TIP:  Find and get familiar picking out four notes (notes may or may not transpose) on the 5th and 6th strings.  They form the intro and a little voicing bridge between verses:  5th string/2nd fret note <b>, open 5th string note <a>, 6th string/3rd fret note <g>, and 6th string/2nd fret note <f#>.  They'll be followed by an (Em).  The first three notes are played as the intro.  The same three notes, plus the last one, the <f#> is played between verses.  For the intro try forming (Em) since that will be the first chord played and then pick the covered 5th string, then lift off and pick the 5th string again, then use your pinky to pick the <g> on the top string and then strum (Em).  For the four in between the verses you'll end with a (B7) so your middle finger will already be on the <b> so hold form and pick the 5th string and move on from there.  Sounds complicated but it's not.  Just try it a few times.}

TIP:  You can play either (B7) or a (B), whichever you prefer.
 
     
